sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Gallus gallus Holocene Turing pigment-ocellus wavelength, 319.2 µm (pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 72.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 solves the Schnakenberg onset wavenumber so λ_c = 319.2 µm exactly at age 0 Ma (Gallus chronoseries 1/1, no predecessor or successor). A single radial harmonic plus a quadratic trend matches the gallery ocellus plate at Pearson r = 0.985 against a trend-only null of lower correlation. The painted scale-bar reader is wrong on this pass (it spans stray bright pixels and reports ~10 µm). There is no Dv sweep, no integrated equal-diffusion ablation, and no computer-vision segmentation of the plate. Overall 72.4/100 (faithfulness 68.3, reproducibility 82.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8be940bbc4e23235f2785d66e06db9da83a65aee; environment: python 3.12.3, note numpy, scipy, pillow, matplotlib, pyyaml, rdflib installed for this run. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 76, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 48, Morphometric validation 62, Source and data traceability 84, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 82. Output judged: docs/media/gallus_gallus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gallus-gallus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8be940bbc4e23235f2785d66e06db9da83a65aee, image/png, 436094 B, 1500×504 px, artifact_sha256 a9d7854ae24967e566ae04c4f936b5a8c06cfb5cddd3f5d8ec4e3e5ed7dc32cf (sha256 a9d7854ae24967e566ae04c4f936b5a8c06cfb5cddd3f5d8ec4e3e5ed7dc32cf), spec_fingerprint d79e485299e3508a55f35819cf41b353933badb10f650ee2ade00ae23887b314. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d79e485299e3508a55f35819cf41b353933badb10f650ee2ade00ae23887b314; artifact_sha256: a9d7854ae24967e566ae04c4f936b5a8c06cfb5cddd3f5d8ec4e3e5ed7dc32cf; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gallus_gallus_turing_wavelength_s0/gallus_gallus_ocellus_specimen.jpg=7e7d58db6bb564eb..., datasets/gallus_gallus_turing_wavelength_s0/gallus_gallus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=5589d95bf0b106f7...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived a finite-wavenumber instability of a homogeneous reaction-diffusion state. | Prum & Williamson (2002) reproduced within-feather bars, spots, and ocelli with reaction-diffusion on a growing feather germ. | Harris et al. (2005) reported Shh/Bmp2 activator-inhibitor interactions during barb-ridge formation in embryonic Gallus gallus.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg slopes at (a, b) = (0.2005, 0.7995), Du = 1, Dv = 16, with γ solved so λ_c = 319.2 µm. | Singleton Holocene chronoseries: age 0 Ma, index 1 of 1, no predecessor and no successor. | Single-harmonic radial reconstruction of the gallery ocellus plate, grown by a Stuart-Landau amplitude in a 12-frame GIF.; transfer_boundary: 319.2 µm is the slot's primordium-scale wavelength, not a length read off the plate's painted 100 µm bar. | The gallery plate is the campaign ocellus image, not a micrograph with a calibrated scale.; does_not_claim: That a blinded prediction of a second feather was tested. | That the painted bar measures 319.2 µm. | That pass 1 already contains a parameter sweep, an integrated ablation, or specimen CV segmentation.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Sweep inhibitor diffusivity Dv at fixed γ and show λ_c(Dv) and the Turing margin R(Dv), including the stable side of onset.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Integrate the Schnakenberg PDE: the critical mode must grow at Dv = 16 and decay under the equal-diffusion ablation Dv = Du.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Segment the real ocellus plate (foreground fraction, structure-tensor coherency, circularity) and compare those measurements to the rendered frame.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Replace the single in-sample harmonic with a held-out multi-harmonic goodness-of-fit (Pearson r, RMSE, KS) and fix the painted scale-bar measurement.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Force-track gallus_gallus_ocellus_specimen.jpg so the SHA-256 pin is in the repository despite the specimen-jpg gitignore.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.724"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second provider on this pass)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

